 "result_text": "I changed `parse_get_bucket_location` in `botocore/handlers.py` so a stubbed client error on `get_bucket_location` should now raise the `ClientError` you asked for. I haven't run your reproduction or the test suite.\n\nThe handler used to read the HTTP response body unconditionally. A stubbed error response has no raw body, which is where the `'NoneType' object has no attribute 'stream'` came from. It now returns early when the parsed response contains an `Error`. That is the same way it already skips when `LocationConstraint` is present.\n\nThe early return also applies to real (non-stubbed) error responses, so those skip the XML parsing as well.",
